[23.220274, "o", "Preprint\r\nVOICE EVALUATION OF REASONING ABILITY: DIAG-\r\nNOSING THE MODALITY-INDUCED PERFORMANCE GAP\r\nYueqianLin♠♣,ZhengmianHu♣,QinsiWang♠♣,YudongLiu♠,HengfanZhang♠,\r\nJayakumarSubramanian♣,NikosVlassis♣,Hai“Helen”Li♠,YiranChen♠\r\n♠DukeUniversity,Durham,NC,USA ♣Adobe,SanJose,CA,USA\r\nCorrespondence: {yueqian.lin@duke.edu,zhengmianh@adobe.com}\r\nABSTRACT\r\nWe present Voice Evaluation of Reasoning Ability (VERA), a benchmark for\r\nevaluatingreasoningabilityinvoice-interactivesystemsunderreal-timeconver-\r\nsationalconstraints. VERAcomprises2,931voice-nativeepisodesderivedfrom\r\nestablishedtextbenchmarksandorganizedintofivetracks(Math,Web,Science,\r\nLong-Context, Factual). Each item is adapted for speech interaction while pre-\r\nservingreasoningdifficulty. VERAenablesdirecttext–voicecomparisonwithin\r\nmodelfamiliesands\r\n\r\n--- Page 2 ---\r\n"]
