[23.86264, "o", "SPEECHPRUNE: Context-aware Token Pruning for Speech Information Retrieval\r\nYueqianLin*1 YuzheFu*1 JingyangZhang1 YudongLiu1 JianyiZhang1 JingweiSun1 HaiLi1\r\nYiranChen1\r\nAbstract DespitethebroadapplicationsofSpeechLLMs,onedesir-\r\nWhile current Speech Large Language Models ablefunctionalityforthesemodelsremainsunexploredin\r\n(Speech LLMs) excel at short-form tasks, they existingwork. Specifically,itisthecapabilityofextracting\r\nstrugglewiththecomputationalandrepresenta- crucial information within long-context audio, which we\r\ntionaldemandsoflongeraudioclips. Toadvance term Speech Information Retrieval (SIR). SIR is particu-\r\nthe model’s capabilities with long-form speech, larlyrelevanttoreal-worldscenarios,whichoftenrequire\r\nweintroduceSpeechInformationRetrieval(SIR), extracting key information from ex\r\n\r\n--- Page 2 ---\r\n"]
